</td>
</tr>
<tr><td colspan="3"><hr /></td></tr>
<tr valign="top">
<td><h2>Glex to present at DIGEX on 6 April</h2></td>
<td><h3>Company news</h3></td>
<td align="right"><h3>2022-03-29 10:26:39</h3></td>
</tr>
<tr valign="top">
<td colspan="3"><p>Chief Commercial Officer Brit Thyberg will present Glex at DIGEX - The Digital Subsurface - at Clarion Hotel Air, Sola on 6 April. The theme of the presentation will be:<br><br>- Unlocking the potential of QEMSCAN and XRD RWI cuttings data through incorporation of metadata, game technology, and interactive workflows.<br>- Examples from the NCS overburden<br><br>About the conference on 5-7 April:<br>Digital technology is enabling the oil & gas industry to completely change the way geoscientists work, how it impacts our daily jobs, and the possibilities that come with it.<br><br>Why?<br>Concrete examples will be presented of how companies are embracing the possibilities within this emerging domain and how they are changing their workflows and approach to the entire value chain from a subsurface perspective.<br><br>For whom?<br>Geoscientists, programmers, and industry professionals working within the subsurface domain in the oil & gas industry.<br>- Oil companies<br>- Service companies<br>- Authorities<br>- Research and educational institutions<br><br>Contacts:<br>Enquiries: contact@glex.no<br>Brit Thyberg, CCO Glex AS, e-mail: brit@glex.no<br>Jørgen Engen Napstad, CEO Glex AS, e-mail: jorgen@glex.no</p></td>
</tr>
<tr valign="top">
<td colspan="3" align="right">
<a target="_blank" href="http://www.glex.no">
http://www.glex.no</a>
<a href="/public/news/20456.jpg">
Digex.jpg</a>
</td>
</tr>
<tr valign="top">
